# =============================================================================
# ERP-Repair multi-tenant reverse proxy (Caddy).
#
# The operator stack (deploy/docker-compose.yml) runs Caddy as the single
# entrypoint for ALL clients. Each client is exactly one site file:
#
#   deploy/caddy/sites/<slug>.caddy      (generated by scripts/add-client.sh)
#
# Caddy terminates TLS (Let's Encrypt via ACME) and proxies traffic to the
# client's API container over the shared `erp_proxy` Docker network:
#
#   Browser
#     │  HTTPS
#     ▼
#   Caddy :443 ──docker-DNS──▶ api-<slug>:3000 ──▶ db (per-client Postgres)
#
# No host ports are published per client — containers communicate over the
# internal erp_proxy bridge by DNS name.
# =============================================================================

{
    email {env.CADDY_EMAIL}
}

# One site file per client (do not edit by hand — use add-client.sh):
import sites/*.caddy
